        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఐతిహ్యం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఐతిహ్యం — aitihyaṁ — \"a legend; lore\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ కోట గురించి ఒక ఐతిహ్యం ఉంది. ā kōṭa guriñci oka aitihyaṁ undi. There is a legend about that fort."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A story handed down by word of mouth, not written in history books."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఐతిహ్యం (aitihyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit aitihya, \"traditional instruction, tradition\" (Monier-Williams), from iti ha, \"thus indeed\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
